OpenDiscordBot
==============

A small, general-purpose discord.js v14 bot. Requires Node.js 22.12 or newer.

Setup
-----

git clone https://github.com/wired420/OpenDiscordBot.git
cd OpenDiscordBot
npm install
cp config.json-default config.json

Edit config.json with your bot token, client id, your user id and any other
settings. In the Discord Developer Portal, enable the "Message Content" intent
for the bot (needed for the ! prefix commands).

npm run deploy      # register the /slash commands with Discord (once, and after changes)
./startup.sh        # start the bot in a detached screen session
npm run dev         # or: run in the foreground, restarting on file changes

Features
--------

Per-server settings are stored in SQLite (data/bot.db) and changed from Discord
with /settings by the bot owner or server administrators. Back up data/ to keep them.

- Rules verification: reacting to the rules message gives a role (/settings verify).
- !help, !ptt / !pushtotalk
- /everyone [message]   ping @everyone (admins, or the role set with /settings everyonerole; logged)
- /setnick [nickname]   set (or reset) the bot's nickname on this server (owner or admins)
- /settings            view/change per-server settings: prefix, log channel, /everyone role, verify
- /server, /whoami
- /reload               reload command files and re-register commands (owner only)

Running as a systemd service (Linux)
------------------------------------

Edit User and WorkingDirectory in opendiscordbot.service, then:

sudo cp opendiscordbot.service /etc/systemd/system/
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable --now opendiscordbot
journalctl -u opendiscordbot -f     # follow the logs

To update: git pull && npm ci --omit=dev && npm run deploy && sudo systemctl restart opendiscordbot
